  "task_completions": [
    "Depending on whether you are looking for descriptive, medical, or flattering terms, here are ten common words used to describe body shapes:\n\n**General & Descriptive**\n1. **Athletic** – Firm and toned, usually implying a person who exercises regularly.\n2. **Slender** – Thin in an attractive, graceful way.\n3. **Curvy** – Having a shapely figure with defined curves (often used for \"hourglass\" shapes).\n4. **Stocky** – Broad and sturdy, usually shorter in stature.\n5. **Petite** – Small and slender (typically used for shorter women).\n\n**Shape-Specific**\n6. **Pear-shaped** – Wider at the hips than at the shoulders.\n7. **Apple-shaped** – Carrying more weight around the midsection/stomach.\n8. **Hourglass** – Balanced shoulders and hips with a narrow waist.\n\n**Broad/Large**\n9. **Burly** – Large and strong; heavily built (typically used for men).\n10. **Plump** – Softly rounded; a polite way to describe someone who is slightly overweight.",
    "Depending on whether you are describing someone in a medical, fashion, or casual context, the words you use will change. Here are ten words describing body shape, categorized by their tone:\n\n### Neutral or Descriptive (Often used in fashion/art)\n1. **Athletic** – Firm and toned; looks like they exercise regularly.\n2. **Slender** – Thin in an attractive or graceful way.\n3. **Curvy** – Having a shapely figure with defined curves (often used for \"hourglass\" shapes).\n4. **Pear-shaped** – Wider at the hips than at the shoulders.\n5. **Petite** – Small and short in stature.\n\n### Descriptive of Fullness (Varying degrees)\n6. **Stocky** – Broad and sturdy; usually short and strong.\n7. **Plump** – Slightly overweight in a soft, rounded way.\n8. **Voluptuous** – Full-figured and attractive (usually referring to women).\n9. **Lean** – Thin but with visible muscle definition; very little body fat.\n10. **Lanky** – Tall and thin, often moving somewhat awkwardly.",
    "Depending on whether you are looking for neutral, positive, or technical terms, here are ten common words used to describe body shape:\n\n### General & Descriptive\n1. **Athletic** – Strong, fit, and muscular.\n2. **Slender** – Thin in an attractive or graceful way.\n3. **Curvy** – Having a shapely figure with defined curves (often used for hourglass shapes).\n4. **Stocky** – Broad and sturdy, usually shorter in height.\n5. **Petite** – Small and slender (typically referring to shorter women).\n\n### Shape-Specific (Geometric)\n6. **Pear-shaped** – Wider at the hips than at the shoulders.\n7. **Apple-shaped** – Carrying more weight around the midsection/stomach.\n8. **Hourglass** – Balanced shoulders and hips with a narrow waist.\n9. **Rectangular** – A straight silhouette where the waist is not very defined.\n10. **Inverted Triangle** – Broader shoulders and narrower hips."
